{"proposal":{"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.9d6ef75f1b5f4ae94e41f5d5.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Footnote 5 specifies paragraph 14's minimum content while preserving its request qualification for demonstration.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.9d6ef75f1b5f4ae94e41f5d5.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The narrow predicate below addresses only whether demonstration is called for; it does not assess confirmation, performance or SFC satisfaction.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"49faf3ddb249393b43d006add21c0e737339ad4cbf775d8c6ec494898f511437","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an in-scope Product Provider, true means the request condition activating paragraph 14 demonstration is satisfied; false means that demonstration has not been activated by a request. Confirmation remains unqualified by a request. Confirmation and demonstration concern management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity. Footnote 5 supplies minimum content: compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and high-confidence assurance that smart contracts have no contract vulnerabilities or security flaws. Paragraph 14 expressly subjects demonstration to SFC satisfaction. Paragraph 15 separately calls for obtaining third-party audit or verification on request; paragraph 16 separately calls for a satisfactory legal opinion supporting the application on request. Neither automatically follows merely from a paragraph 14 request.","family_ids":["exceptions"],"parent_id":null,"revision_reason":"Without a request, confirmation remains called for but demonstration under paragraph 14 is not activated. This differs from reading footnote 5 as an independent minimum demonstration duty. Absence of a request proves neither fulfillment nor SFC acceptance.","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0